   "message": "SEB-301: the Aider builder takes every ready backlog job; one-call runs by hand only (#658)\n\n* SEB-301: the Aider builder takes every ready backlog job; one-call runs by hand only\n\nSeb, 24 Oct: the agents sat idle from 23 Oct with ready jobs in the queue.\n- aider_builder.py: the pilot limit to items 1 to 3 is gone. It takes the top\n  ready job with files listed and no track or `track: aider`. Next up: 5a\n  (Australia to India), then 7b, then 18a.\n- one_call.yml: no schedule. It built nothing live since 20 Oct.\n- check_runner_health.py watches aider_builder.yml, so the watchdog does not\n  go red for the one-call runner being off.\n- CLAUDE.md describes the builder as it now runs, and where hard jobs go.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LK5gd53j6Yqo8BMPPjJxFg\n\n* SEB-301: Aider self-test matches the new picking rule (no pilot limit, track: claude left alone)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LK5gd53j6Yqo8BMPPjJxFg\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
